  "description": "Single storey side to rear extension (demolition of garage)",
  "development_type": "Other house holder developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development, by reason of the single storey side‑to‑rear wrap‑around extension, its scale, siting and form, would result in an unsympathetic, incongruous, bulky and obtrusive form of development that would erode the characteristic separation between the dwelling and garage, reduce openness, block intended views towards rear garden greenery, disrupt the intended symmetry with the opposing property, and cause the loss of original elongated side stair window that is a consistent designed feature on these semi-detached houses. As such, the development would be detrimental to the character and appearance of the host dwelling, the visual amenities of the area and the Pinnerwood Park Estate Conservation Area, contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3 and HC 1 of the London Plan (2021), Policies GR1, HE 1 and HE2 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021 – 2041), and the adopted supplementary planning documents: the Residential Design Guide (2010) and Pinnerwood Park Estate Appraisal, Management Strategy and Design Guide (2009).&lt;/p&gt;"
